      <section class="guide-article__section">
        <h2>Getting Started: Unboxing Your Libersens Product</h2>
        <p>When your Libersens order arrives, it comes in plain outer packaging — no product names or branding on the outside. Inside, you'll find your product nestled in a soft storage pouch alongside the charging cable and a brief care card.</p>
        <p>Before your first use, take a moment to inspect the product. The silicone surface should be smooth and uniform. Remove all packaging materials, including any protective films over charging ports or indicator lights.</p>
        <div class="guide-article__callout">
          <strong>First thing to do:</strong> Charge your product fully before use. A full charge typically takes 60 to 90 minutes and ensures you get the full range of intensities from the start.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-article__section">
        <h2>Charging: What You Need to Know</h2>
        <p>Libersens products use magnetic USB charging. Align the cable with the charging port at the base — you'll feel a gentle click when it connects. A small LED indicator will pulse while charging and switch to steady when complete.</p>
        <ul class="guide-article__list">
          <li>Charge on a flat, dry surface away from moisture</li>
          <li>Avoid charging overnight once fully charged to preserve battery health</li>
          <li>If the product hasn't been used for a while, a full recharge before use is recommended</li>
          <li>A full charge typically provides 2 to 3 hours of use depending on intensity settings</li>
        </ul>
        <p>If the LED doesn't respond when you connect the cable, try reversing the cable orientation — magnetic ports work in both directions on most models.</p>
      </section>

      <div class="guide-article__image-break">
        <img src="{{ 'libersens-product-wearable.png' | asset_url }}" alt="Libersens She Bell wearable product" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="600">
        <p class="guide-article__image-caption">The She Bell is designed for all-day wear — lightweight, discreet, and hands-free.</p>
