      <section class="guide-article__section">
        <h2>First Use: Finding Your Comfort</h2>
        <p>There's no single right way to use a Libersens product — the goal is to find what feels easy and natural for you. Here's a gentle framework for your first session.</p>
        <p><strong>Start with the lowest intensity.</strong> Every Libersens product begins at mode one on a single press. The lowest setting is gentle enough for first-time users and still effective for experienced ones. There's no rush to move up.</p>
        <p><strong>Take your time with positioning.</strong> For wearable products like She Bell, a minute spent on positioning is worth ten minutes of adjustment later. The contoured shape has a defined orientation — consult the care card diagram if you're unsure.</p>
        <p><strong>Cycle through modes slowly.</strong> A single button press moves you forward through intensity levels. To turn off, hold the button for two seconds. You can return to mode one at any point by briefly removing and reinserting the product, or by cycling to the end of the sequence.</p>
        <div class="guide-article__callout">
          <strong>Good to know:</strong> Libersens products are whisper-quiet at all settings. At the lowest intensity, they produce less than 40dB — quieter than a library.
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-article__section">
        <h2>Cleaning: Simple Habits After Every Use</h2>
        <p>Keeping your product clean is the most important maintenance step, and it takes less than two minutes. Body-safe silicone is non-porous, which means it doesn't harbour bacteria the way porous materials can — but it still needs proper cleaning.</p>
        <p><strong>What to use:</strong> Warm water and a fragrance-free intimate toy cleanser, or a plain mild soap. Avoid anything with alcohol, petroleum, or bleach — these can degrade the silicone surface over time.</p>
        <p><strong>How to clean:</strong> Apply a small amount of cleanser to your hand, lather gently over the silicone surface, rinse thoroughly under warm running water, and pat dry with a clean lint-free cloth. Leave to air dry fully before storing.</p>
        <p><strong>What to avoid:</strong></p>
        <ul class="guide-article__list">
          <li>Submerging the charging port or LED indicator in water</li>
          <li>Abrasive cloths or sponges that may scratch the surface</li>
          <li>Dishwashers, boiling water, or UV sterilisers not rated for silicone</li>
          <li>Storing before fully dry, which can cause moisture buildup</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="guide-article__section">
        <h2>Storage: Keeping It Private and Protected</h2>
        <p>Each Libersens product includes a soft drawstring storage pouch. Use it. The pouch protects the silicone surface from dust, lint, and contact with other materials — some of which can cause surface degradation over time.</p>
        <p>Store your product in a cool, dry location away from direct sunlight and heat sources. A bedside drawer, a small toiletry bag, or a dedicated pouch box all work well. Avoid storing near sharp objects or with silicone-incompatible materials such as certain plastics.</p>
        <p>For travel, the pouch is compact enough to fit in a toiletry bag. The product looks like any personal care device from the outside. If you're travelling internationally, the charging cable is a standard USB type and doesn't require adapters in most regions.</p>
      </section>

